    "hint": "The argument of a logarithm has to be greater than zero, so start by writing the expression inside the logarithm above zero. Solving that for $x$ is where the direction of the inequality gets decided, because $x$ has a minus sign in front of it, and the vertical asymptote then stands at the boundary value the domain begins at.",
